Letter ranges are defined in the same way as numeric ranges. @tbl-regex-range summarizes the range patters most commonly used in Polars. Square brackets can also include symbols or other non-alphanumeric characters, such as `[@%$]`:

| **_Range pattern_** | **_Purpose_**                                                                      |
| :------------ | :--------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `[0-9]`       | Match any number.                                                            |
| `[a-z]`       | Match any lowercase letter.                                                  |
| `[A-Z]`       | Match any uppercase letter.                                                  |
| `[A-Za-z0-9]` | Match any lowercase or uppercase letter, or any number.                      |
| `[A-z]`       | Match any ASCII character; generally not used because it matches everything, including symbols  |                                                          |

: Regex range patterns. {#tbl-regex-range}{tbl-colwidths="[25,75]"}

